omx-contract (3.19.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * omx-contract 3.19.0 changelog: name every user-facing PR since 3.18.1,
    date it at the cut
  * omx-contract 3.19.0: one release for #44, #52, #73, #79 and #82
  * release.yml: the Prove job installs the pinned shape generators, as
    ci.yml does
  * domain.mts: each doc comment sits on the constant it describes
  * domain directory: its catalogs/<lang>.json sit beside the document
  * domain document: $schema must be JSON Schema 2020-12; the docs claim only
    what the loader does (cross-domain $ref and version validation are #84)
  * ownership gate: say what a new word is
  * ownership gate: word sets, schema enums, loader read, moved-back and
    duplicate refusals, fetched base, bootstrap that ends (A2 review of #82)
  * ownership gate tests first: word sets, schema enums, moved back,
    duplicates, bootstrap end, unfetchable base (red against the first gate)
  * contract-dir: the ownership gate holds word sets and schema enums, reads
    through the loader, refuses an unreadable base (A2 review of #82)
  * ownership gate: every data/ item owned here or moving out, the moving-out
    list only shrinking (omx-contract#81)
  * contract-dir: the ownership gate, what omx-contract owns and what only
    moves out (omx-contract#81)
  * contract dir: the loader reads a domain document (oneOf/const words) as
    the classic items; its renders are byte-equal
  * contract dir: a words item of a domain is a oneOf of const words (spec)
  * contract dir: a domain is one OpenAPI-3.1-style document at
    <contractdir>/<domain>/, its owner is info.x-owner, no major in the path
    (spec)
  * vocabulary: the display sources' and placements' docs name omx-panel's
    tool
  * render: a doc comment on every vocabulary macro, so the doc gate holds
  * vocabulary: PANEL_DISPLAY_SOURCES and PANEL_PLACEMENTS declared here,
    since 3.20.0
  * test: the panel display sources and placements are required as vocabulary
    (red)
  * vocabulary: PANEL_DISPLAY_KINDS gains time_response (code 4); its doc
    names omx-panel's tool
  * test: the panel display kinds carry time_response at code 4
  * shapes: a oneOf's words get their macro, patternProperties are refused by
    name, and a title two shapes share is refused by both files
  * shapes: prose reaches a C comment with its doxygen command characters
    escaped, and the data package's expected file list reads the shapes from
    the tree's root
  * shapes test: the Python render arm skips only where no generator is
    installed and CI is not set, so a red py --check step is a red test there
  * shapes: the C render is refused where it would be wrong, both generators
    are held to their pins at run time, the house header
  * render --check: the hand-written CLAP kind vectors and the shapes' Python
    render are named beside the json, lv2 and py renders
  * spec: the dated copy of the typed-contracts document is removed; the
    move's deletion side, left behind by a pathspec commit
  * spec: the typed-contracts document moves to
    docs/typed-contracts-shared-behaviour.md and states the console's facts
    without pointers into it
  * shapes installed: the schemas under share/omx-contract/shapes, the
    TypedDicts as omx_contract.shapes.<name>, and CI holds the three renders
    by the pinned generators
  * shapes: a document's shape is one JSON Schema under shapes/, rendered to
    TypeScript, Python and C by render --shapes and held by --check
  * spec: the owner rules the shapes decisions; JSON Schema now, TypeSpec
    only possibly later; the shapes directory and where a schema is
    installed, as lane S1 builds it
  * spec: the owner rules behaviour as C + WebAssembly for every JavaScript
    runtime; shapes stay proposed with the TypeSpec-as-authoring note
  * spec: typed contracts and shared behaviour, one shape source and one
    implementation bound per runtime
  * descriptors: the vectors' readers named without a private path
  * clap-kind-vectors: every default inside its range, and the wider stepped
    range, the lone enumeration flag and a half step as cases
  * share/omx-contract/clap-kind-vectors.json: the thirteen vectors,
    installed beside scale-vectors.json
  * test: the CLAP kind vectors are one table every reader is held to (red)
  * docs/descriptors: a scanned CLAP parameter's kind is read by one rule,
    held by a vectors table
  * param-contract: pc is percent, with no range of its own
  * doxygen gate: a Doxyfile that suppresses what it counts, or drops a
    setting it needs, is a finding by key (read back through doxygen -x); a
    header hiding code under @cond is refused by name, as is a @file outside
    a doc comment; an empty DOXYGEN_BASE is refused; the JSON writer's put
    macro moves to file scope so doxygen can read its block (a define inside
    a function body takes none); build/ ignored
  * render: the documentation law names the gate's refusals (a @cond, a @file
    outside a doc comment, a Doxyfile that suppresses), its limit (a false
    preprocessor condition), --list, --update, DOXYGEN_BASE and the exit codes
  * doxygen gate: the tracked headers only, so a stray file counts on neither
    side; --update writes the baseline only when it lowers, refused by name
    otherwise; no Doxyfile, no baseline, no header refused by name; the set
    arms (a swapped line red by both names, a dropped newline no change); the
    README names the gate
  * param-units test: the define's trailing doc is read past, the regex
    literal's slashes escaped
  * omx_param_units.h and omx_json_write.h documented: a docs line per unit
    token in the data, so the header's defines and the json carry it; the
    writer's three functions name each parameter, its owner and the return,
    its own put macro is hidden from the reader; the baseline falls 670 to 636
  * omx_contract_limits.h documented from the data: every limit, scalar,
    list, set, readout and rate define carries its item's doc, unit and
    since, a sheet's leaves as one member group, the rates function its
    parameters and return; the resolved item keeps since, so the json render
    carries it; the one doxygen-line helper spells the vocabulary, hints and
    owner headers too; the baseline falls 719 to 670
  * render: a define's or a function's doxygen block stands above its line, a
    member's one line trails it
  * doxygen-check: a base ref git cannot read is a refusal, exit 2, never a
    pass with no base; a commit with no baseline yet says so
  * doxygen gate: make doxygen-check holds the installed headers'
    undocumented public declarations to docs/doxygen-baseline.txt (719
    today), red on a new one, a stale line and a line added against main; CI
    runs it and its red-first test
  * render: every installed header opens with a @file block, so doxygen reads
    its declarations; the JSON writer's own block too, its escape spelled so
    doxygen reads no command in it
  * render: the documentation law of the installed headers: a @file block per
    header, a doxygen block per public declaration spelled from the item, the
    undocumented ones a baseline that only shrinks
  * render: the C text helpers in their own module; the frozen limits
    renderer goes
  * test: the C text helpers are in their own module, the frozen limits
    renderer is gone (red first)
  * Remove the backward-compatibility machinery
  * test: no backward-compatibility machinery is left (red first)
  * Remove the schema history and the floor-understated check
  * test: the reader keeps no schema history (red)
  * docs: the reader keeps no schema history
  * schema/history: schema 3.18.0 frozen; owner-requires reads only its own
    directories
  * test: the host's installed contract directory never reaches
    owner-requires (red first)
  * test: every schema minor a release shipped is frozen in schema/history
    (red first)
  * vocabulary: every words item renders an X-macro; PANEL_DISPLAY_KINDS
    declared here
  * test: words items render an X-macro; panel display kinds are declared
    here (red first)
  * override schema: the family enum lists utility, held against
    PANEL_FAMILIES
  * utility family: the c, ts and json renders and the six catalog sentences
  * plugin-vocabulary: the panel families list ends with utility
  * panel.json: the utility panel family joins PANEL_FAMILIES
  * ci: no bookworm package cells (no new bookworm releases)
  * ci: the heavy workflows run by dispatch and tags; the fast checks alone
    on a pull request
  * ci: the trigger gate on every pull request, red
  * Makefile: the shared checks' checkout is OPENMIXER_DOTGITHUB
  * Artifact retention: explicit retention-days, 30 on a tag and 2 otherwise
  * tests: npm pack runs on a staged copy, never in ROOT: its prepack rebuilt
    lib/ under the parallel suite (#39)
  * build-lib is a file target, and the suite removes its scratch directories
    (#39)
  * translate --owner: resolve a tree's requires, read schema/codes.json, or
    refuse by name
  * test: translate --owner of a tree that requires a package or declares its
    codes in schema/ (red: false undeclared)
  * contract codes: contract.requires.unresolved and
    contract.owner.codes-unlocated, declared with their catalog entries
  * translate --owner: resolve a tree's requires, read its declared code
    locations, or refuse by name
  * release 3.19.0: the verb and role fixtures state the schema floor of this
    release
  * release 3.19.0: a catalog entry may be by: same (schema 3.19.0)
  * ca catalog: give the 51 plain entries their by form, RESOURCE_UNITS.bytes
    by: same, reword the two refused glossary forms
  * schema: catalogEntry gains by: same with its source hash; readers keep it
    and never regenerate it
  * test: a by: same catalog entry validates, is read, is stale on a changed
    source and is never regenerated
  * docs: a catalog entry may be by: same, the same word as the English
    source sentence

